Coherent Solutions
is a digital product engineering company focused on empowering business success. Our global team of 1700+ talented professionals collaborate seamlessly to deliver innovative solutions that drive measurable business impact. Headquartered in Minneapolis, USA, the company’s core competencies across 10 locations worldwide include product software development, IT consulting, data and analytics, machine learning, mobile app development, DevOps, Salesforce, and more.

We grow a team of advisors, not just order takers, and strive to make the company a place for career growth and opportunities. If you want to grow your core competencies, share your passion and be sure that every contribution is evaluated, we are on the same page.

Company Background

Our client is a leading global data center provider delivering hyperscale and edge infrastructure solutions across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific. With 80+ data centers in 20+ countries, they partner with industry leaders such as Google, Oracle, NVIDIA, and Microsoft Azure to power the world’s digital infrastructure. Recognized as a USA TODAY Top Workplace for four consecutive years, the company continues to expand its global footprint and customer ecosystem.

Project Description

The specialist will join a newly established team supporting the company’s transition to an automation-first and AI-first operating model. The role focuses on delivering scalable and secure automation solutions across enterprise business functions while maintaining a high degree of technical ownership and independence.

Technologies

UiPath
Automation Anywhere / Blue Prism / Power Automate / similar RPA platforms
JavaScript / .NET
MuleSoft
Alteryx / Workiva / similar low-code/no-code automation platforms
APIs
Scripting
SQL, Azure SQL / other relational DB
NoSQL DB

What You'll Do

Design, develop, deploy, and enhance automation solutions supporting business processes across finance, operations, IT, and other enterprise functions;
Work independently with minimal functional requirements, defining automation approaches, system integrations, and technical solutions for both custom-built and commercial enterprise systems;
Evaluate automation platforms and select the most appropriate tools for each use case;
Design and develop intelligent process automations and workflows using low-code/no-code platforms such as Alteryx, Blue Prism, UiPath, Power Automate, and Workiva;
Build and maintain system integrations using APIs and middleware platforms such as MuleSoft;
Design and work with relational and NoSQL databases, including Azure SQL, to support automation logic, data persistence, and reporting;
Apply system architecture principles to ensure automation solutions are scalable, maintainable, and aligned with enterprise standards;
Apply master data management principles to maintain data consistency and integrity across automated processes;
Collaborate with stakeholders to identify automation opportunities and improve business efficiency;
Monitor, troubleshoot, and optimize deployed automations to ensure reliability and performance;
Document automation designs, data flows, and integration patterns to support long-term maintainability;

Job Requirements

3+ years of professional experience in automation engineering, system integration, or a related technical role;
Hands-on experience with UiPath or, alternatively, strong experience with another RPA platform (Automation Anywhere, Blue Prism, or Power Automate) combined with JavaScript or .NET programming experience;
Strong knowledge of relational databases and SQL, including experience with Azure SQL or another relational database platform;
Experience designing and consuming APIs for system integration;
Practical scripting experience;
Strong system architecture skills and experience designing end-to-end automation solutions;
Understanding of master data management principles and enterprise data consistency;
Understanding of product management principles, including prioritization and requirements documentation;
Experience supporting multiple business functions within enterprise environments;
Ability to prioritize multiple initiatives and deliver solutions in a fast-paced environment;
Readiness to maintain at least four hours of daily overlap with EST;
RPA platform certification obtained within the past three years, preferably UiPath, is a plus;

What Do We Offer

Resources and opportunities for self-education in technical and non-technical areas;
Access to internal conferences and meetups for knowledge sharing and learning from industry experts;
Medical insurance;
Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;
Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;
Referral program for bringing in new talent.

If this opportunity excites you, send us your resume!

Please, note, that we will consider all the applications with due respect, but only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.

Please take your time to see Coherent Solutions Privacy Policy for Job Applicants for details on how we process your personal data: https://www.coherentsolutions.com/privacy-policy-for-job-applicants

