ABOUT THE COMPANY:

ALTEN is a multinational group created more than 30 years ago, specialized in consulting services, information technology and engineering services to the main companies in the market. We achieved a turnover of more than 4.14 billion euros in 2024 and now have 57,700 employees, 88% of whom are consulting engineers.

ABOUT PORTO & POSITION:

To support our European intensive growth, the Group has decided to build a Center based in Porto with the aim to provide administrative and financial support to the European subsidiaries.
In this context, we are looking for a skilled C#/.NET Developer to join the Integration teams (aka "middleware") within the ALTEN Group Information Systems & Technology (IS&T) department.
The Integration team is responsible for designing, building, and supporting all ALTEN Group application-to-application digital data flows. Because end-to-end business processes span multiple applications, connecting applications together is essential to delivering a seamless digital experience for end users while ensuring reliability and performance for the company.
The ideal candidate must have significant experience and strong skills in C# and .NET development, preferably in a Microsoft Azure cloud environment.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:

Integration & C#/.NET Development:

Build and maintain end-to-end application-to-application digital flows using Azure Integration Services (Logic Apps, Data Factory, Service Bus, API Management, Azure Functions);
Develop and maintain complex integration logic using C# and .NET technologies, particularly when solutions exceed low-code/no-code capabilities;
Build scalable and reliable solutions leveraging Azure Functions and Azure App Services;
Enhance traditional software solutions with AI-powered capabilities whenever relevant and valuable,

Documentation:

Write technical specifications and architecture documentation;
Ensure all developments and integrations are properly documented according to best practices;

Continuous Improvement:

Propose technical enhancements and development best practices;
Promote the controlled and relevant adoption of AI-assisted development tools and methodologies;
Perform quality control on deliverables, including code reviews and technical documentation;

Support & Resolution:

Assist in User Acceptance Testing (UAT), bug resolution, and enhancement implementation with appropriate cutover plans;
Support production environments and contribute to the continuous improvement of existing integrations and applications;

This description considers the main responsibilities; it is not exhaustive.

Minimum/Essential Skills/Qualifications

PROFILE:

Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field;
At least 3 years of experience in C# and .NET development;
Professional level of English;
Strong proficiency in C# and .NET development;
Experience with Visual Studio;
Familiarity with Git and CI/CD pipelines;
Strong interest in learning and mastering Azure Integration Services (Logic Apps, Data Factory, API Management, Service Bus, Azure Functions, etc.);
Initial experience with Azure development environments such as Azure App Services or Azure DevOps is a plus;
Initial experience with AI-assisted software development tools (GitHub Copilot or similar) is appreciated;
Ability to understand and define stakeholder needs;
Excellent communication skills;
Highly motivated, analytical, and adaptable in an international environment;
Passion for digital transformation and emerging technologies.

PERKS:

Meal allowance;
Health insurance;
Transportation allowance;
Extra holiday days;
Professional development and growth opportunities.

